WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.807
This is the heart of the chapter:

2
00:00:01.807 --> 00:00:05.725
what happens if you create Microsoft's
template exactly as published.

3
00:00:05.725 --> 00:00:08.638
The targeting is good, so
it's kept as the model.

4
00:00:08.638 --> 00:00:11.321
But the published example
lists only two roles

5
00:00:11.321 --> 00:00:13.799
where Learn's own
procedure wants fourteen.

6
00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:16.839
It grants plain multifactor
sign-in instead of the

7
00:00:16.839 --> 00:00:20.313
phishing-resistant strength,
and the two can't be combined.

8
00:00:20.313 --> 00:00:24.717
And it excludes a line of display text
where an object identifier belongs,

9
00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:28.400
which the admin center would
replace for you, but a script won't.

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.580
Each of these is pinned by a test.
